d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-1407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,78,13⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-1407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,78,-13⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,3,0⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{49}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 3 & 0 \\\\ -x & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(x+0)j+(0+3x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-x,3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ 10{x}^{2}+9 & =49 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2,$ $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0118fa4be877af9d984d96913b8c4eb3649797d2aa3621bd31fccb9b4080a716" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-1406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u=3i-2k$ and $v=-2i+j+5k.$ Determine $u\\times v.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-1406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-(3\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot (-2))j+(3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =(0+2)i-(15-4)j+(3-0)k \\\\  & =2i-11j+3k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-1406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef4c79489825927f20cb39471f088d40ce9a02efd3b0d42ca81aa883b95487a"} {"question" "q-1406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-1406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2i+11j-5k"] ["math" "2i+3k"] ["math" "2i-11j+3k"] ["math" "2i-11k"] ["math" "7i-11j+3k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-1406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2i-11j+3k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-1407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨0,1,6⟩$ and $b=⟨13,0,0⟩.$ Find $a\\times b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-1407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 13 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 13 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 13 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 0-6\\cdot 0)i-(0\\cdot 0-6\\cdot 13)j+(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 13)k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-78)j+(0-13)k \\\\  & =78j-13k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-1407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef4c79489825927f20cb39471f088d40ce9a02efd3b0d42ca81aa883b95487a"} {"question" "q-1407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-1407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-6,-78,13⟩"] ["math" "⟨-6,0,-13⟩"] ["math" "⟨-6,78,-13⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,78,-13⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,78,13⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-1407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,78,-13⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-19786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨2,0,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{13}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-19786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(6x-8)j+(0-2)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-(6x-8),-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-(6x-8))^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36{x}^{2}-96x+64+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ \\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77} & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+77 & =13 \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+64 & =0 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-24x+16 & =0 \\\\ (3x-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-4 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-19786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef4c79489825927f20cb39471f088d40ce9a02efd3b0d42ca81aa883b95487a"} {"question" "q-19786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-19786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\frac{4}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-19786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,3,0⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{49}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 3 & 0 \\\\ -x & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(x+0)j+(0+3x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-x,3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ 10{x}^{2}+9 & =49 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2,$ $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef4c79489825927f20cb39471f088d40ce9a02efd3b0d42ca81aa883b95487a"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,4,5⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{33}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4-0)i-(x-5)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4,5-x,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(5-x)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+(25-10x+{x}^{2})+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+57}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{33} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+57} & =\\sqrt{33} \\\\ {x}^{2}-10x+57 & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}-10x+24 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =4,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=4,$ $x=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef4c79489825927f20cb39471f088d40ce9a02efd3b0d42ca81aa883b95487a"} {"question" "q-282276" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282276" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1379263cfc8033546d2be2c76154ac0d"} {"question" "q-282276" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064610/state.json" "file_sha256" "f5c7cf7fb973bb3b791acc20582e985a1